WEBVTT


00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.740
잘 먹겠습니다

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.300
에 이모가

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.600
에잉 그지요 엘록스 윌 버 there's a reason

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.000
first Japanese meals are light

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.580
rice in a light wooden bowl

00:00:19.581 --> 00:00:22.801
with fish pickled vegetable and a simple soup

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.620
holding the bowl just keeps the rice from falling

00:00:25.621 --> 00:00:28.601
so putting it down eating like a dog

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:30.980
but Korea is different

00:00:30.981 --> 00:00:34.401
Korean used to get almost all their calories from rice

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.700
and to eat that much rice they always had soup

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:40.661
so spoons were almost with a spoon

00:00:40.662 --> 00:00:44.681
you won't drop a single grain so the bowl stays on the table

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:48.640
there was no reason to lift your bowl unless you were beggar

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.840
that's why Korean developed ceramic and metal bowl

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:56.320
heavier and harder than wood but cleaner and they last forever
